      "rationale": "ERA5 precipitation at Jesen\u00edk (50.276N, 17.181E) for Sep 12-16, 2024 totals 445.9 mm (39.1+102.8+171.0+110.8+22.2), well over the claimed 300 mm, with a peak daily value of 171.0 mm on Sep 14 (overall peak across the full Sep 1-17 window was also 171.0 mm). This confirms extreme, flood-level rainfall. GDACS corroborates an Orange-level flood alert for 'Austria, Czech Republic, Germany, Poland, Romania, Slovakia' from 2024-09-12 to 2024-09-18, 49 km from the point, plus a nearby Green flood event in Poland 15 km away (Sep 13-15) \u2014 consistent with the widely-reported Storm Boris disaster. GloFAS river discharge at the nearest cell (50.275N, 17.225E) peaked at 63.27 m3/s on Sep 15, a 13.8x rise over the 4.57 m3/s baseline, ranked #1 (highest) among 16 years of annual maxima \u2014 strong independent confirmation of extreme flood conditions. No nearby Meteostat weather station (within 75 km) or European gauge (France/UK network only) had data, so those two tools are inconclusive/not applicable here, but the precipitation, GDACS, and GloFAS evidence together strongly support the claim.",
