      "claim": "Storm Boris caused flooding that spread across Poland, Czechia, Austria and Slovakia in mid-September 2024.",
      "verdict": "supports",
      "rationale": "GDACS recorded an Orange-alert flood event named 'Flood in Austria, Czech Republic, Germany, Poland, Romania, Slovakia' running 2024-09-12 to 2024-09-18, only 16 km from the query point, plus separate Green-alert entries for 'Flood in Poland' (Sep 13-15) and 'Flood in Slovakia' (Sep 14-16) \u2014 directly corroborating the claimed multi-country flood footprint. Precipitation (ERA5) near the Czech/Poland border (50.43N,16.65E) totaled 206.7 mm over the 20-day window with a peak of 53.9 mm on Sep 15; near Austria (48.3N,15.6E) totals reached 276.5 mm with a peak of 102.5 mm on Sep 14 \u2014 both extreme multi-day rainfall totals consistent with Boris's slow-moving rain bands. GloFAS discharge confirms flood-level river response in both countries: the Czech/Poland river cell (50.475N,16.675E) peaked at 84.7 m\u00b3/s on Sep 17, 4.3x its 60-day baseline (19.75 m\u00b3/s), ranked #1 (highest) of 11 years of annual maxima; the Austrian river cell (48.375N,15.625E) peaked at 8,490.8 m\u00b3/s on Sep 16, 3.4x baseline (2,516.7 m\u00b3/s), also ranked #1 of 11 years. These record-setting, multi-year-high discharge peaks in both countries, paired with the GDACS multi-country flood catalog entry and extreme rainfall totals, meet the bar for flood-level conditions. (find_nearest_water_body returned a server error with no data; get_station_observations and get_european_river_gauges found no station/gauge coverage near this remote point within range \u2014 these are inconclusive gaps, not contradicting evidence, and are outweighed by the GDACS and GloFAS findings.)",
